        {"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"Pedagogical continuity","value":"Documented pedagogical activity spans the institution from its 1987 founding period through the 2012 didactic reform and into the current multidisciplinary teaching ecosystem."},
        {"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"Highly qualified educator evidence","value":"Multiple documented university and teacher-training degrees, preschool- and primary-teacher qualifications, special-education credentials, Montessori and motopedagogy training, Waldorf qualification, music-pedagogy and music-therapy credentials, academic leadership and multi-decade teaching careers support an institution-level characterization of a highly qualified educator and specialist network."},
        {"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"Pedagogical system evidence","value":"The jubilee publication and 2012 reform documentation describe a shared pedagogical concept, differentiated teaching based on Hungarian-language competence and explicit use of bilingualism research."},
        {"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"Qualification scope rule","value":"Highly qualified is a qualitative institution-level characterization supported by multiple named examples. It must not be interpreted as a claim that every historical contributor held an identical degree, regulated credential or employment status."},
        {"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"Employment inference rule","value":"A historical teaching, advisory, coordination or program role is not automatically an employment relationship."}
